# Next.js build output (apps/console). All generated, all gitignored — and `next-env.d.ts` and the
# compiled service worker are written by the toolchain in a format Prettier disagrees with, so a
# `pnpm lint` run that happens after a build would fail on files nobody authored.
#
# Deliberately scoped to Next's own output only: this file is new, and widening it further would
# silently change what `pnpm format` reformats across the whole repo.
**/.next/
apps/console/next-env.d.ts
apps/console/public/sw.js
apps/console/public/sw.js.map
apps/console/public/swe-worker-*.js

# Vite production build output (apps/authz-ui, story #406). Same reasoning as the Next.js block
# above: `dist/` is generated, gitignored (apps/authz-ui/.gitignore), and its content-hashed
# JS/CSS bundle plus the built `sw.js` are minified/toolchain-formatted, not authored -- a `pnpm
# lint` run against a working tree that already has a local `pnpm --filter authz-ui build:web` in
# it would otherwise report false regressions on files nobody wrote by hand.
apps/authz-ui/dist/

# Other build/codegen output that isn't hand-authored, so Prettier has no business reformatting
# it (and shouldn't be a source of `pnpm lint` noise the moment it's produced or regenerated
# locally): the typst-render sidecar's compiled output, the authz-rpc cratestack-generated client,
# the api-rest openapi-ts-generated client, and any Storybook static build anywhere in the repo.
apps/typst-render/dist/
packages/authz-rpc/generated/
packages/api-rest/src/client/
**/storybook-static/

# `apps/lci`'s Next.js type shim, same case as `apps/console/next-env.d.ts` above -- written by the
# toolchain on every build, gitignored, in a format Prettier disagrees with. It was missing from
# this list only because it did not exist yet when the console entry was added.
apps/lci/next-env.d.ts

# `apps/governance-auth`'s single-file build output (vite-plugin-singlefile inlines every asset
# into one HTML file). Same reasoning as the `apps/authz-ui/dist/` block above.
apps/governance-auth/dist/

# The Storybook accessibility baseline (#443). MACHINE-WRITTEN by
# `packages/ui-web/scripts/a11y-storybook-gate.mjs --update`, which emits `JSON.stringify(…, 2)`.
# Prettier would collapse its one-element `rules` arrays onto a single line, so every regeneration
# would leave the tree unformatted and `pnpm lint` red until someone ran `pnpm format` — a trap for
# exactly the person who just did the right thing and ratcheted the baseline down.
packages/ui-web/a11y-storybook-baseline.json
